[%cachewrite 2945] The red rook on b6 attacks my cannon on e6 along rank 6, and
nothing defends it. Worse, capturing it would also be check: 车八平五 (Rxe6+)
hits my king through the empty e7 square. - **Why not attack first:** I looked
at 炮9进3 (i3i0) and 马7退6 (g2f0), which set up a mate with cannon on i0 and
knight on f0. Both let red take the cannon with check first. Red then drops the
rook to e0 to block, so the attack gains nothing and I lose material. - **Why
not other squares on the e-file:** If the cannon leaves the e-file, red gets
车平五 with check, and the cannon is lost anyway. - **Why e7:** Retreating to
e7 puts the cannon next to my king, which protects it. It also blocks the
e-file check and keeps shielding the king. The i0/f0 mating idea stays
available. If red later plays the knight to d6, I can play 炮5平6 (cannon to
d7), using that knight as a screen to check along the d-file. } 52. 马七进六
